at in this far-flung  future  loki had essentially killed everybody on  earth now while the asgardians  themselves were fine  this more or less coincided with gore  the god butcher in this far-flung future  basically taking his army of you know  living abyss  minions more or less and descending on  to asgard and so those asgardians who  were not killed  were captured and forced into the  service of of gore whose intention we'll  talk about here in a second  and basically what it meant was that all  father thor was basically the only  asgardian that was left he was  ultimately captured and then forced into  the subservience of gore but really more  just kind of taunted with the fact that  all the asgardians had been killed by  gore and gore's own kind of grim  satisfaction in knowing that he had  essentially won now in terms of what  gore's motivation  was because of the fact that going  across the universe and killing  virtually every god he could find was a  lengthy process  he had the age to do it the problem with  this is that one of the things that had  happened over the course of the thor god  of thunder story is that there were god  refugees which is to say those  individuals who had heard what gore was  doing  and then basically went into hiding and  this ultimately meant that gore  could not satisfy his ultimate goal to  kill every single god across the  universe throughout all space and time  and so what he ended up doing was  basically working to construct something  called the god bomb and the whole idea  behind this is he would detonate it in  the time stream and the explosion would  emanate outward from whatever point in  time it detonated  and essentially kill every god across  the entirety of the universe's history  regardless of where they were hiding  and so what this did is it ultimately  led to thor from the past  teaming up with thor from the present  along with thor from the future right so  three generations of thor  all facing off against gore